1
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:14,600
A gift box is 20 centimetres long, 15 centimetres wide and 10 centimetres high.

2
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:20,160
You want to cover every face with wrapping paper, with no overlaps.

3
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:21,970
How much paper do you need?

4
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:25,270
Here is a hint: imagine opening the box out flat.

5
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:28,820
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:32,090
A box has 6 faces, in 3 matching pairs.

7
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:40,690
The top and the bottom are each 20 by 15: that is 300 square centimetres each, 600 for the pair.

8
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:46,090
The front and the back are each 20 by 10: 400 for the pair.

9
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:50,940
The 2 ends are each 15 by 10: 300 for the pair.

10
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:58,110
600 plus 400 plus 300 is 1,300 square centimetres of paper.

11
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:01,460
Remember: a net is a 3D shape opened out flat.

12
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:06,230
The net of a cuboid has 6 rectangles, in 3 matching pairs.

13
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:10,740
The surface area of a 3D shape is the total area of all its faces.

14
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:13,900
It is the same as the area of its net.

15
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:20,250
For a cuboid, find the area of the 3 different faces, add them, and double the total.

16
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,900
Surface area is an area.

17
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:25,960
So it is measured in square units, not cubic units.

18
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:28,580
A cube has 6 identical square faces.

19
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:32,770
So its surface area is 6 times the area of 1 face.

20
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:38,680
For a cube with sides of 3 centimetres, 1 face is 3 times 3, which is 9.

21
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:42,100
6 times 9 is 54 square centimetres.

22
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:42,790
Your turn.

23
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:47,170
What is the surface area of a cube with sides of 2 centimetres?

24
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:50,440
Pause the video and try it.

25
00:01:50,490 --> 00:01:53,220
1 face is 2 times 2, which is 4.

26
00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:54,780
There are 6 faces.

27
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:58,360
6 times 4 is 24 square centimetres.

28
00:01:58,410 --> 00:01:59,690
Here is the method.

29
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:04,890
Step 1: sketch the cuboid, and label its length, width and height.

30
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:08,980
Step 2: find the area of the 3 different faces.

31
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:14,600
Step 3: add them, and double the total, because opposite faces are equal.

32
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:17,980
Step 4: give the answer in square units.

33
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:25,280
Find the surface area of a cuboid that is 8 centimetres by 5 centimetres by 2 centimetres.

34
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:29,610
The 3 different faces are 8 times 5, which is 40.

35
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,090
Then 8 times 2, which is 16.

36
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:35,020
And 5 times 2, which is 10.

37
00:02:35,070 --> 00:02:36,190
Add them: 66.

38
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,780
Double it: 132 square centimetres.

39
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:40,510
Your turn.

40
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,270
A cuboid is 3 by 3 by 1.

41
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:44,100
What is its surface area?

42
00:02:44,150 --> 00:02:47,470
Pause the video and try it.

43
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,490
The 3 different faces are 9, 3 and 3.

44
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:51,950
They add up to 15.

45
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,330
Double it: the surface area is 30 square units.

46
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:03,000
A box with no lid is 40 centimetres long, 25 centimetres wide and 10 centimetres high.

47
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:05,800
How much cardboard is needed?

48
00:03:05,850 --> 00:03:12,860
There is only 1 face of 40 by 25, the bottom: 1,000 square centimetres.

49
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:18,230
The front and back are 2 times 40 times 10, which is 800.

50
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:23,210
The ends are 2 times 25 times 10, which is 500.

51
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:27,180
The total is 2,300 square centimetres.

52
00:03:27,230 --> 00:03:31,110
A cube has a surface area of 216 square centimetres.

53
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:33,780
Find the length of its side.

54
00:03:33,830 --> 00:03:35,970
A cube has 6 equal faces.

55
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:37,990
216 divided by 6 is 36.

56
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:41,260
So each face has an area of 36.

57
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,640
6 times 6 is 36.

58
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:45,680
So the side is 6 centimetres.

59
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:49,970
A room is 5 metres long, 4 metres wide and 2.5 metres high.

60
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:54,040
You paint the 4 walls, but not the floor or the ceiling.

61
00:03:54,090 --> 00:03:56,270
What area do you paint?

62
00:03:56,320 --> 00:04:00,490
2 walls are 5 by 2.5: 2 times 12.5 is 25.

63
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:06,080
The other 2 walls are 4 by 2.5: 2 times 10 is 20.

64
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:09,840
25 plus 20 is 45 square metres.

65
00:04:09,890 --> 00:04:13,290
Find the surface area of a cuboid, 5 by 4 by 2.

66
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:14,970
Here is Rosa's working.

67
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:17,580
Which line goes wrong first?

68
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:18,740
Line 2 is wrong.

69
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:20,260
That is only 3 faces.

70
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:25,740
A cuboid has 6 faces, because each face has a matching one opposite.

71
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:27,270
Double the total.

72
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:30,540
2 times 38 is 76 square units.

73
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:34,010
Take an ice cube with sides of 2 centimetres.

74
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:37,800
Its surface area is 24 square centimetres.

75
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:42,490
Now cut it into 8 small cubes, each with sides of 1 centimetre.

76
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:44,650
Each has a surface area of 6.

77
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:48,180
Together, that is 48 square centimetres.

78
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:51,900
It is the same amount of ice, but 2 times the surface.

79
00:04:51,950 --> 00:04:53,270
Heat gets in faster.

80
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:56,640
That is why crushed ice melts so quickly.

81
00:04:56,690 --> 00:04:57,950
One last question.

82
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,750
A cube has a surface area of 150 square centimetres.

83
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,280
How long is its side?

84
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:07,020
Pause the video and work it out.

85
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:09,120
150 divided by 6 is 25.

86
00:05:09,170 --> 00:05:11,680
Each face has an area of 25.

87
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:13,510
And 5 times 5 is 25.

88
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:16,700
So the side is 5 centimetres.

89
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:20,800
To remember: surface area is the total area of all the faces.

90
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:23,090
It is the area of the net.

91
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:28,030
For a cuboid: find the 3 different faces, add them, and double.

92
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:31,450
For a cube: 6 times the area of 1 face.

93
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,980
The units are square units.

94
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:39,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.5 on Camday.
